WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.010
In 1995, India's GDP per
person was 375 dollars.

2
00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:12.390
By 2025, it was 2,702 dollars:
about seven times as much,

3
00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:15.590
in current dollars, not
adjusted for prices.

4
00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:20.230
In 2025 alone, the economy
grew by 7.6 per cent.

5
00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:24.310
Electricity now reaches
99.9 per cent of people,

6
00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:27.090
up from 60 per cent in 2000.

7
00:00:27.140 --> 00:00:29.070
So who has gained from all this growth?

8
00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:30.910
Almost everyone?

9
00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:32.930
The cities more than the villages?

10
00:00:32.980 --> 00:00:34.790
And what has it cost?

11
00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:38.810
In this mission, you'll measure how health
and schooling have changed over thirty

12
00:00:38.860 --> 00:00:39.790
years.

13
00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:43.470
Then you'll weigh those gains
against what growth has cost.

14
00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:46.790
Your mission: evaluate who has
gained from India's growth,

15
00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:48.270
and at what cost.
